  "description": "QAKJEU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C192 H252 Cl2 N12 Nd11 O72 P6 S12 1+,Cl1 1-,7(C3 H7 N1 O1),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd7 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd8 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd9 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd10 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd11 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.826-4.808 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.78-145.82°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd11(BSC4A)3(PhPO3)6(Cl)2(OH)4(DMF)12]Cl·7DMF·2CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
